<BaseLayout title="Professional Vacuum Tube Testing | Antique Radio Salvage" description="Professional vacuum tube testing and matching using Amplitrex, Hickok, TV-7, MAXIPREAMP, Sencore and B&K test equipment." current="testing">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Professional Tube Testing</p><h1>Testing that goes beyond “good” or “bad.”</h1><p class="lead">Measurements are selected to suit the tube type and intended use, with clear results for collectors, audiophiles, musicians, repair professionals and sellers.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><div class="stack">
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Why testing matters</h3><p>A simple emission result does not tell the entire story. Depending on the tube, meaningful evaluation may include shorts, leakage, gas, plate current, mutual conductance, balance between sections and comparison with expected operating values.</p></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Measurements and checks</h3><div class="checklist"><div class="check">Visual inspection</div><div class="check">Shorts</div><div class="check">Leakage</div><div class="check">Gas / grid current</div><div class="check">Plate current</div><div class="check">Mutual conductance</div><div class="check">Emission</div><div class="check">Section balance</div><div class="check">Matched pairs</div><div class="check">Matched quads</div></div></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Test equipment</h3><p>Our equipment includes the Amplitrex AT-1000, a calibrated TV-7A/U, Hickok 539-series equipment, MAXIPREAMP II, Sencore MU150, B&amp;K 747B and other testers and fixtures. No single tester is best for every tube, which is why the equipment and method are selected for the job.</p></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Common applications</h3><p>Pre-sale verification, amplifier troubleshooting, matching output tubes, checking vintage inventory, evaluating inherited tubes and documenting desirable audio or transmitting tubes.</p></div>
    <div class="notice">Please contact us before shipping tubes. We will confirm that the tube types are supported, discuss pricing and provide packing and mailing instructions.</div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact/">Request tube testing</a><a class="btn secondary" href="https://www.ebay.com/itm/256884606545" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View testing listing ↗</a></div>
  </div><aside class="sidebar"><div class="image-shell"><img src="/images/tube-testing-poster.png" alt="Professional vacuum tube testing service" /></div><div class="content-card" style="margin-top:20px"><h3>Before contacting us</h3><p>List the tube numbers, quantity and what you need to learn—for example, basic condition, detailed measurements, a matched pair or documentation for resale.</p></div></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
